  "requiredChecks": ["CI Gate", "Merge Gate"],
  "release": {
    "about": "The owner approves at the release boundary, not at a merge into develop: promotion into main, a release branch or tag, and a contract broadcast on a live network. Promotion into main is his manual step for now, and nothing enforces it yet: the main ruleset requires a pull request and CI Gate but no review, the release branch and tag rulesets require signed commits only, organization admins can bypass all three, and agents act through his GitHub account. Agents tag a release or broadcast on a live network only when he asks in that session, and the guards ask before a live broadcast; a manual production deploy keeps its own out-of-band confirmation (AGENTS.md). Enforcement waits until agents run under their own GitHub identity, when a required review on main can do it. The kit's merge-policy schema has no field for a gate by branch or environment, so the merge-settings tool does not apply this entry. A merge into develop is itself a deploy that this boundary does not cover, which the owner accepted on 16 Nov 2026: every push to develop starts a Fly deploy of the production Agent, so Agent changes go live once they merge on proof. Vercel deploys the QA app's production and the client and admin staging sites from develop too, unless its ignore step (scripts/ops/vercel-ignore.mjs) finds nothing a site is built from changed since that site's last deployment.",
    "approvalAt": ["main", "release/*", "tags v*", "live-network contract broadcasts"]
  },
  "tiers": {
    "critical": {
